{{Portrait}}
Tick is a {{Rarity|Super Rare}} [[Brawler]] who has the lowest health of any Brawler and a very slow reload speed, but has a long range and an inconsistently high damage output. He was the 27th Brawler added to the game. He attacks by lobbing three mines over obstacles that explode on contact with an opponent or after a delay. His Super detaches and launches his head, which chases after the nearest enemy and explodes, dealing high damage and knocking enemies back while also destroying obstacles. His first Gadget, Mine Mania, doubles the amount of mines that his next attack fires. His second Gadget, Last Hurrah, grants him a temporary shield before he explodes, dealing damage and knocking enemies back. His Mythic Gear, Thicc Head, increases the health of his Super. His first Star Power, Well Oiled, allows him to self-heal sooner than normal. His second Star Power, Automa-Tick Reload, decreases his attack's reload time. His Hypercharge, Headstrong, makes his next Super deploy and follow enemies faster, dropping 6 mines upon exploding, which deal very high damage each.

==Attack: Minimines==
{{Quote|Tick lobs a cluster of mines that separate before landing. The mines explode on contact with a target, or after a few seconds.}}When Tick attacks, he lobs a long-ranged projectile over obstacles that after 0.9 seconds splits into three mines that spread over an area. The mines explode on contact with an opposing target or after a two-second delay with a radius of 1.56 tiles. The projectile travels slowly in the air, and Tick's reload speed is very slow; however, the damage of all mines is immense, and the attack's effective range is extremely long. The spread of the mines increases the further away they are thrown: at minimum range they are spaced 1.33 tiles from the attack's center, and this distance expands by up to 90% at max range. It takes the same amount of time for an attack to land regardless of the distance from Tick.

==Super: Headfirst==
{{Quote|Tick detaches and launches his head. After landing, the head hops toward the nearest target and explodes on contact!}}When Tick uses his Super, he detaches his head and launches it over obstacles. After landing, the head chases after the nearest enemy (including those in bushes) and explodes, dealing high damage, knocking enemies back by 2.4 tiles, and destroying obstacles in a 2-tile explosion radius. If the head is destroyed before reaching a target, it still explodes normally. Once close enough to enemies, the head will try to explode, but if it fails its attack, it will attempt to attack again after a 1-second cooldown. If there isn't any target that the head can chase down, it will stay next to Tick.

==Gadgets==
===Mine Mania===
{{Quote|Tick's next attack fires 6 mines. Cooldown: 15 seconds.}}
{{Gadget|1}}
Upon activation, Tick's next main attack fires six mines instead of three, which deals double the usual damage in total. Like his regular attack, the mines' spread increases or decreases depending on the distance thrown. A Gadget symbol will glow above Tick's head signaling the Gadget's usage, as well as a glowing joystick. This Gadget's cooldown begins after the attack is used.

===Last Hurrah===
{{Quote|Tick gains a 50% shield for 1 seconds. After that, it bursts out for 1360 damage. Cooldown: 15 seconds.}}
{{Gadget|2}}
Upon activation, Tick gains a 50% damage reduction shield for 1.05 seconds and explodes in 1 second, dealing the damage of Tick's single mine to enemies and knocking them back 3 tiles in a radius around him. Tick can still move while this Gadget is active. This Gadget's cooldown begins after the explosion detonates.

==Mythic Gear: Thicc Head==
{{Quote|Tick's Head gets 1000 extra health.}}{{Gear|Filename=TickGear}}
With this Gear equipped, Tick's head gains 1000 extra health.

==Star Powers==
===Well Oiled ===
{{Quote|When Tick takes no damage and doesn't attack, he starts recovering health 2 seconds faster than normal.}}
{{StarPower|1}}
Tick's auto-regeneration now starts 1 second after being damaged or attacking instead of the usual 3 seconds.

===Automa-Tick Reload===
{{Quote|Tick's reload time is 9% shorter.}}
{{StarPower|2}}
Tick reloads 0.22 seconds faster, reducing his reload time by 9%.

==Hypercharge: Headstrong==
{{Quote|Tick quickly deploys his head, charging enemies faster and leaving behind 6 of his minimines on explosion.}}{{Hypercharge}}
When activated, Tick's next Super is deployed quicker and follows enemies faster. After his head explodes, no matter if it is destroyed by enemies or it comes in contact with enemies, 6 mines will drop 2.67 tiles around the explosion's center, in a similar pattern to his Mine Mania Gadget. These mines each deal the same damage and recharge his Super as much as his head's explosion. Tick also gains a 20% speed boost, as well as a 5% damage and shield boost.

